# Everything this package ships, and nothing else.
#
# A `.pubignore` does not add to `.gitignore` — it replaces it. Everything the
# repository keeps out of git has to be named again here, or it lands in the
# archive: written without the lines below, this one went from one megabyte to
# forty-seven, all of it build output.
#
# The documents stay: the README links into them forty-eight times, and a link
# that only works on GitHub is half a document. The example stays: it is what
# pub.dev shows on its own tab, and the fastest way to see the kit work.
#
# The tests do not. They are the largest thing here — one file of them is three
# hundred kilobytes — and nobody who depends on the kit runs them. Nor do the
# scripts that guard the repository against itself.
test/
tool/

# What git already keeps out, said again.
build/
coverage/
.dart_tool/
.pub-cache/
.pub/
.packages
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
**/doc/api/
**/ios/Flutter/.last_build_id
migrate_working_dir/
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
.atom/
.buildlog/
.history
.svn/
.swiftpm/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
*.class
*.log
*.pyc
*.swp
.DS_Store
